; requires_system on a real ABIv11 machine.
;
; Six runs, and the reason there are six is that any one of them alone can be
; passed by a check that does the wrong thing:
;
;   1. sdllopan, real package, real index. Its three requirements -- SDL,
;      crt, stdlib -- are all met here, so it must install. A check that
;      refused everything would look correct on run 2 alone.
;   2. req-test-missing. A requirement no machine provides, on a machine of the
;      RIGHT ABI, so the ABI gate cannot be what refuses it. Mainline would
;      stop an ABIv11 package earlier and prove nothing about this code.
;   3. req-test-satisfied. dos.library, which every AROS has. The control for
;      run 2: without it, a refusal there might just mean the field refuses
;      anything it is given.
;   4. req-test-undetermined. A requirement type the client cannot decide. It
;      must install ANYWAY, warn, and leave the doubt in the registry.
;   5. lopan actually starting. Installing is not running.
;   6. removal, to show it takes its own files and nothing else.
;
; Nothing here removes or modifies a system library. The negative case is made
; by asking for a library that was never there, not by taking one away.

FAILAT 21
Copy PAYLOAD:PKGONE RAM:apkg
Copy PAYLOAD:REQIDX RAM:req-index.json
Protect RAM:apkg +e

Echo "== requires_system, ABIv11 =="
RAM:apkg --version

Delete SYS:PkgReq ALL FORCE QUIET
MakeDir SYS:PkgReq
Delete RAM:reports ALL FORCE QUIET
MakeDir RAM:reports

Echo "*N-- 1. sdllopan: three requirements, all met here --"
RAM:apkg --root SYS:PkgReq update
RAM:apkg --root SYS:PkgReq search sdllopan
RAM:apkg --root SYS:PkgReq --expect 0 --run-id req-1-sdllopan --machine onetest --report RAM:reports/req-1.json install sdllopan
Echo "*Nthe registry entry, with the verdicts in it:"
RAM:apkg --root SYS:PkgReq info sdllopan

Echo "*N-- 2. a library nothing provides: must refuse, must name it --"
RAM:apkg --root SYS:PkgReq --index RAM:req-index.json --expect 13 --run-id req-2-missing --machine onetest --report RAM:reports/req-2.json install req-test-missing
Echo "*Nthe cache must not contain it -- the refusal came BEFORE the download:"
List SYS:PkgReq/cache

Echo "*N-- 3. control: a requirement every AROS meets --"
RAM:apkg --root SYS:PkgReq --index RAM:req-index.json --expect 0 --run-id req-3-satisfied --machine onetest --report RAM:reports/req-3.json install req-test-satisfied

Echo "*N-- 4. undetermined: installs, warns, and records the doubt --"
RAM:apkg --root SYS:PkgReq --index RAM:req-index.json --expect 0 --run-id req-4-undetermined --machine onetest --report RAM:reports/req-4.json install req-test-undetermined
Echo "*Nthe registry must say undetermined, not satisfied:"
RAM:apkg --root SYS:PkgReq info req-test-undetermined

Echo "*N-- what is installed --"
RAM:apkg --root SYS:PkgReq list

Echo "*N-- 5. the point of all this: does it run? --"
Echo "starting lopan; close its window to continue"
SYS:PkgReq/sdllopan/lopan

Echo "*N-- 6. removal takes its own files and nothing else --"
RAM:apkg --root SYS:PkgReq --expect 0 --run-id req-6-remove --machine onetest --report RAM:reports/req-6.json remove sdllopan
RAM:apkg --root SYS:PkgReq list
Echo "*Nthe system libraries must still be there:"
List LIBS:SDL.library
List LIBS:crt.library

Echo "*N-- reports --"
List RAM:reports
Type RAM:reports/req-2.json
Echo "== end =="
